--- A stop inside a script's `later` work ends the work, not the script,
--- and says why (spec, Background Work: "a failure stops it ... the
--- notice says why"): the interpreter, running the work inline, had ended
--- the program with it, and the compiled program's thread had ended in
--- silence, the script going on as if nothing had happened. Both print
--- the stop, then the script goes on.
fn work[]
    xs = [1]
    log[xs[5]]

later[work]
while running[work]
    sleep[10]
log['after the work']
